ighted;¦layout ‚¤textÙ'Neither turneth he back from the sword.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ The quiver rattleth against him,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$The glittering spear and the shield.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2He swalloweth the ground with fierceness and rage:¦layout ‚¤textÙ9Neither believeth he that it is the sound of the trumpet.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ$He saith among the trumpets, Ha, ha;¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And he smelleth the battle afar off,¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ.The thunder of the captains, and the shouting.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter'«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ Doth the hawk fly by thy wisdom,¦layout ‚¤textÙ'And stretch her wings toward the south?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'Doth the eagle mount up at thy command,¦layout ‚¤textºAnd make her nest on high?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%She dwelleth and abideth on the rock,¦layout ‚¤textÙ0Upon the crag of the rock, and the strong place.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!From thence she seeketh the prey,¦layout ‚¤text½And her eyes behold afar off.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"Her young ones also suck up blood:¦layout ‚¤textÙ&And where the slain are, there is she.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse